    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699094/stores-purchasing-officer": {
      "title": "Stores Purchasing Officer - 2 part time vacancies available",
      "description": "Stores Purchasing Officer - 2 part time vacancies available Job No.: 699094 Location: 0.6 part-time at Alfred Hospital Campus (1000 - 1424), 0.8 part-time at Clayton Campus (0800-1500) Employment Type: 2 x Part-time positions available, one at 0.6 and one at 0.8 Duration: 6 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $79,430 - $84,963 HEW 4 plus 17% employer superannuation Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity We have two exciting six-month, part-time fixed-term opportunities for Stores Purchasing Officers, one working 0.6 FTE at the Alfred Hospital Campus and one 0.8 FTE at the Clayton Campus. Working as part of the Purchasing Services Team, you’ll provide high-quality administrative, purchasing and inventory services to support the effective operation of the P2P Stores. You’ll be responsible for maintaining stock levels, ordering and receiving goods, managing inventory and responding to queries, while providing excellent service to staff, students and other stakeholders. This is a hands-on role with an important focus on safety, compliance and continuous improvement. You’ll provide advice on the safe storage, handling and disposal of hazardous materials, including dangerous and temperature-sensitive products, while ensuring purchasing and inventory activities align with University policies, tax requirements and occupational health and safety standards. You’ll also contribute to analysing usage trends and improving processes to support efficient and responsive stores services. Please note this position is 5 days on site. About You You’ll bring strong administrative and organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, maintain accurate records and deliver operational processes efficiently. A relevant tertiary qualification, substantial relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience will be highly regarded. You’ll also have strong computer literacy, including experience with Microsoft Office and purchasing or inventory management systems such as SAP. You’ll be a customer-focused and practical team player who can communicate confidently with a diverse range of people and provide helpful, timely advice. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills are important, along with the ability to identify issues, interpret data and develop effective solutions. Experience with chemicals, laboratory consumables and equipment, and the safe handling of hazardous materials, and a current forklift license, will be highly regarded. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible working arrangements. Whilst this role is worked 100% on-site, we have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This role requires current valid work rights for Australia. Monash University invites applications from candidates who can demonstrate valid and current Australian work rights. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: June Ellis Lau, Purchasing Manager, juneellis.lau@monash.edu / 03 9905 2639 Position Description: Stores Purchasing Officer Clayton Campus Stores Purchasing Officer Alfred Hospital Campus Applications Close: Monday 26th of October 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
