    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698835/human-resources-business-partner": {
      "title": "Human Resources Business Partner",
      "description": "HR Business Partner Job No: 698835 Location: 211 Wellington Road, Mulgrave and Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12 months fixed-term Remuneration: $145,481 - $160,58 total remuneration package pa HEW Level 08 (inclusive of $124,343 - $137,251 base salary pa and 17% employer superannuation) Partner with extraordinary minds and leaders shaping tomorrow Join a high-performing HR Business Partnering team Balance ambition and well-being through flexible, tailored working options Monash University is a global leader ranked among the world's top universities. With annual revenue exceeding $3 billion and campuses across 5 countries, Monash combines the commercial scale, operational complexity, and rigor of a major global enterprise with a deeply values-driven mission. Learn more about Monash . The Opportunity We are seeking a HR Business Partner on a 12-month fixed-term contract to join our HR ecosystem. Operating within a portfolio-based model supporting academic or professional divisions, this high-impact role requires strong coaching capability, alongside strategic advisory, organisational design, and industrial relations experience to navigate complex environments and transformation. Key Responsibilities Strategic Business Partnering & Advising: Serve as a trusted HR partner, advisor and coach to leadership teams across an assigned faculty, division, or school. Provide high-level consulting, practical guidance, and tailored HR solutions to navigate complex workforce dynamics and support organisational objectives. Workforce Planning & Change Delivery: Partner with leadership to support organisational design, succession planning, and change management initiatives. Play a key role in strategic workforce planning, analysing workforce data to identify talent needs, mitigate pipeline risks, and build an agile workforce responsive to shifting academic or operational priorities. Complex Employee Relations & EA Application: Manage complex employee and industrial relations matters and undertake workplace investigations within an Enterprise Agreement (EA) environment. Collaborate with specialised ER teams and leaders to interpret policy and legislation, manage risk, and foster constructive workplace relations. HR Projects & Continuous Improvement: Contribute to broader HR and university-wide transformation projects and continuous improvement initiatives. Incorporate external research, industry benchmarks, and progressive HR insights to elevate HR service delivery. Innovation & Digital Mindset: Champion process optimisation and the adoption of digital tools (including AI) to streamline HR practices, challenge legacy approaches, and drive operational excellence. Cross-Functional Collaboration & Knowledge Sharing: Work collaboratively with Monash HR colleagues, and Centers of Excellence (CoE) to deliver seamless, consistent HR services. Support and share knowledge with peers to build collective capability across the HR function. What we are looking for: Matrix Savvy & Systemic Thinker: Strong ability to navigate and partner within a large, complex matrix environment operating across Shared Services and Centers of Excellence Executive Presence & Coaching Mindset: Excellent interpersonal and consulting skills with the proven ability to build strong strategic relationships, influence outcomes, and provide sound coaching to client leaders Commercially Minded & Purpose-Led: Sharp business acumen balanced with an unwavering alignment to a values-driven, purpose-led culture. Digital Curiosity & Innovation: A forward-thinking, adaptable mindset with genuine enthusiasm for leveraging AI, tech optimisation, and creative problem-solving. Industrial & ER Expertise: Sound judgment and confidence navigating Enterprise Agreements, complex ER matters in unionised environments. Analytical & Evidence-Based: Strong data instincts with the natural ability to turn complex workforce metrics into clear, compelling strategic narratives. Collaborative leader: A genuine commitment to supporting and developing junior peers, sharing knowledge, and elevating overall team capability. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed Be part of our story. Work with us to #ChangeIt . Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply To apply, submit your CV along with a cover letter (maximum two pages) addressing your suitability to this position. Key Selection Criteria responses are not required. Please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs' . Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodiverse people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Jo Dallas, Senior Manager Talent Acquisition, 9905 6121 Applications Close: Thursday 29 October 2026, 11:55PM AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698886/research-manager": {
      "title": "Research Manager",
      "description": "Research Manager Job No.: 698886 Location: Monash Medical Centre Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 15 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $124,343 - $137,251 pa HEW 8 plus 17% super Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Build partnerships and enable excellence. Bring expertise, influence and innovation. The Opportunity Drive research strategy and impact as the Research Manager, this will include being the key person in supporting school leadership to deliver strategic and operational research priorities. From grant development and post-award management to research planning, reporting and performance measurement, you’ll provide expert advice that helps shape a high-performing research environment. Working across the Faculty, Research Office, Hudson Institute of Medical Research, Monash Health and external funding bodies, you’ll establish a strong precinct approach to research support. You’ll manage complex research programs and projects, oversee budgets, risk, compliance and quality assurance, and identify opportunities for collaboration, funding and business development. We’re looking for an experienced research professional with strong project and operational management capabilities, highly developed analytical and organisational skills, and the ability to influence and build consensus across complex environments. Your specialist knowledge, strategic mindset and collaborative approach will help advance research priorities and deliver meaningful outcomes for the School and its partners. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We make tangible contributions because our purpose is clear; to deliver positive economic, social and environmental impact in resolving the global challenges of our age. At the core of achieving this purpose is the diversity of our staff. We welcome and value everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. When you come to work, you can be yourself, be a change-maker and develop your career in exciting ways. This is why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Please address the Key Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description within your cover letter, explaining how your skills, experience and qualifications make you a suitable candidate for the position. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Amanda McFarlane, Manager, School of Clinical Sciences - 0401 086 962 Position Description: Research Manager Applications Close: Thursday, 29th October at 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
