    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699161/lecturer-or-senior-lecturer-in-paramedicine": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Paramedicine",
      "description": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Paramedicine Job No.: 699161 Location: Peninsula campus Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.6) Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: Pro-rata of $123,138 - $146,228 pa Level B (plus 17% employer superannuation) or Pro-rata of $150,841 - $173,931 pa Level C (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Paramedicine Join a collaborative community advancing Paramedicine education Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Department of Paramedicine is seeking a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer to join the team to contribute to high-quality education, research and professional activities within the Department. The position will support the delivery of contemporary Paramedicine education, preparing students for professional practice through relevant curriculum, teaching and learning resources, assessment and student supervision, while contributing to the academic objectives of the Department, School and Faculty. The role will contribute to subject and course development and delivery, including teaching, assessment and student engagement. Research activities will include project participation, scholarly publications and supervision of honours and postgraduate students. At Senior Lecturer level, the position will also provide academic leadership, support educational innovation, research collaboration and funding, and strengthen relationships across the University and Paramedicine profession. We are seeking someone with a relevant postgraduate or doctoral qualification and current or eligible registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). The ideal appointee will also bring strong clinical experience, a record of teaching and research achievement and the ability to work effectively across academic and service settings. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to the advancement of Paramedicine education, research and professional practice at Monash University, and applications are encouraged. The successful applicant will be appointed at either Level B or Level C, commensurate with qualifications and relevant experience. Please specify in your cover letter the level that you are applying for. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Kelly-Ann Bowles, Head of Department, Kelly-Ann.bowles@monash.edu Position Description: Level B Lecturer Level C Senior Lecturer Applications Close: Thursday 29 October 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699400/monash-education-phd-scholarship-hitting-the-limits-intersectional-sexisms-in-australian-universities": {
      "title": "Monash Education PhD Scholarship: Hitting the limits - Intersectional sexisms in Australian universities",
      "description": "Monash Education PhD Scholarship: Hitting the limits - Intersectional sexisms in Australian universities Job No.: 699400 Faculty: Faculty of Education Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 3.5-year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $41,000 p/a Principal Supervisor(s): Associate Professor Emily M. Gray Associate Supervisor(s): Professor Jacqueline Ullman (Western Sydney University), Associate Professor Lucy Nicholas (Western Sydney University) The Opportunity Applications are invited from outstanding domestic candidates for a fully funded research-based PhD scholarship, based at the School of Education and Culture at the Faculty of Education in Melbourne, Australia. The successful applicant will work alongside a team of researchers from across Australia who are working on an Australian Research Council funded project entitled Hitting the Limits: Intersectional sexisms in Australian universities . The scholarship will fund a project that examines LGBTIQA+ academics’ institutional locations, experiences and private and professional means of support within Australian universities. Applicant are encouraged to develop their own research project in relation to the following key questions: Where are LGBTIQA+ academics in Australia located in terms of discipline and geographical location? Do LGBTIQA+ academics in Australia feel welcome within their workplaces? What support mechanisms and/or strategies to LGBTIQA+ academic staff draw upon in their private and professional worlds? The project Hitting the Limits responds to the limits of Australian university culture by examining the conditions that limit social cohesion in relation to gender. The project generates new theoretical, cultural and practical knowledge about how experiences of intersectionality, gender, power and complexity shape universities. Joining our thriving research community at the School of Education and Culture and Monash Faculty of Education which is consistently ranked as the number 1 education faculty in Australia, your PhD project will offer an opportunity to connect with students and leading experts across the globe. Candidate Requirements To be eligible you must: be an Australian citizen/New Zealand citizen or Australian permanent resident have the necessary qualifications, such as a research masters or honours year to meet the selection requirements into the doctoral program (see Monash University PhD entry requirements) be enrolling full time and on campus not already hold a PhD In its assessment, the selection committee will prioritise applicants with significant knowledge of feminist and queer theories and LGBTIQA+ people and communities. LGBTIQA+ people and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. The successful applicant will be expected to enrol by February 2027. However, there may be some flexibility to the date of commencement. Enquiries Faculty of Education Graduate Research Office Email: edu-gradresearch@monash.edu Submit an Expression of Interest (EOI) Scholarship applicants should submit a brief, 3-4 page research proposal that outlines how you will address the research topic. Please refer to the Faculty’s guideline section 2, Prepare your research proposal, to assist with this. Submit your EoI via this link . Applications Close: Monday 30 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697511/senior-full-stack-engineer": {
      "title": "Senior Full Stack Engineer",
      "description": "Senior Full Stack Engineer Job No.: 697511 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 2-year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $110,527 - $121,227 pa HEW Level 07 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Monash Institute of Railway Technology (IRT) is the premier track and vehicle research centre in Australia and an internationally recognised leader in railway engineering solutions. 100% industry-funded through contractual work with over 150 global client organisations, IRT translates cutting-edge applied research into real-world industrial impact. We are seeking a Senior Full Stack Engineer to join IRT’s Innovation Team. In this role, you will lead the research, development, deployment, and management of software platforms and AI models powered by smart sensors across rolling stock and track systems. You will play a pivotal role in creating client-facing applications and real-time decision-support tools that convert complex sensor data into actionable insights for railway operators. Key Responsibilities Full Stack & AI Platform Development: Design, build, and deploy end-to-end AI applications, backend APIs, data pipelines, and user interfaces that enable data visualisation, analysis, and decision-making from condition monitoring systems. Edge & Computer Vision Integration: Deploy AI, computer vision, laser profiling, LiDAR, and camera-based systems on edge devices operating under constrained resources or intermittent connectivity. Advanced Signal & Sensor Processing: Implement advanced real-time data processing techniques, sensor fusion (multimodal data including inertial, LiDAR, radar, and imaging), parallel processing, multithreading, and GPU/distributed computing. Software Governance & MLOps: Establish mature product development practices, including CI/CD automation, software architecture standards, testing protocols, data traceability, and model confidence metrics. Project Delivery & Client Engagement: Lead assigned project scopes and technical deliverables to ensure completion within budget and timeline while building strong relationships with clients and industry partners. Field Support & Operations: Provide expert technical support during system commissioning, deployment, and operational troubleshooting, including occasional travel for site visits. About You Qualifications: A Bachelor’s degree in Engineering with relevant subsequent experience, postgraduate qualifications, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Full Stack Proficiency: Demonstrated expertise in end-to-end software development, including backend services, APIs, databases, front-end interfaces, and tools such as Python , Flask , Docker , AWS , and GitLab . AI & Computer Vision Experience: Proven experience with computer vision systems, machine learning workflows, MLOps, and edge processing optimisation. Multimodal Sensor Expertise: Hands-on experience ingesting, filtering, and preprocessing multimodal sensor data (e.g., LiDAR, radar, inertial, imaging). Project & Stakeholder Management: Excellent analytical problem-solving skills, with a track record of managing technical project deadlines and communicating complex technical concepts to diverse stakeholders. Operational Readiness: Flexibility to travel within Australia and overseas, perform field work/out-of-hours shifts as required, and satisfy pre-employment railway medical and drug screenings About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Dr. Nithurshan Nadarajah, Deputy Director - Innovation, nithurshan.nadarajah@monash.edu Position Description: Senior Full Stack Engineer Applications Close: Tuesday 27 October at 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699118/postdoctoral-research-fellow": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow Job No.: 699118 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $86,195 - $116,981 pa Level A (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Are you a PhD graduate in Structural or Mechanical Engineering looking to push the boundaries of computational mechanics, fracture modelling, and experimental validation? Join us for a targeted 12-month research initiative bridging high-performance computing (HPC) , advanced ABAQUS finite-element modelling, and hands-on laboratory testing. Reporting to a Professor in Structural Engineering, you will lead the development and validation of multi-scale fracture mechanics models. In this role, you will bridge numerical simulation with physical experiment, developing automated Python workflows, running parametric studies on HPC clusters, and validating predictions against experimental results. What You’ll Do Advanced FEA and Automation: Build, verify, and validate multi-scale models using ABAQUS linked with user-defined material/element subroutines, writing Python scripts for simulation automation, data processing, and workflow optimisation. Develop Machine Learning (ML) models: Train ML models based on published literature, experimental data, and FEA results to support optimization of advanced materials. Bridge Theory and Experiment: Support mechanical testing (setup, instrumentation, and data acquisition) to validate numerical predictions and contribute to machine learning and optimisation activities. Mentorship and Collaboration: Provide technical guidance and scripting support to PhD students, co-author journal manuscripts, and contribute to research funding applications. Deliver High-Impact Outcomes: Drive the project toward key deliverables, including a reusable modelling workflow, a structured simulation dataset, and top-tier journal submissions. What You Will Bring Qualification: A PhD in Structural Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Core FEA and ML Skills: Proven expertise in finite-element modelling with ABAQUS, grounded in solid and fracture mechanics (e.g. multi-scale modelling of composite laminates or concrete, phase-field fracture modelling) and experience with ML models. Programming Capabilities : Strong Python skills for automation, data analysis, and workflow tool development, including experience with ML and optimisation Research Drive : Excellent communication skills, a collegiate mindset, and a strong track record of producing clear reports and publications. Experimental Testing: Experience with experimental testing using mechanical loading machines. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Dr. Fatemeh Azhari, Senior Lecturer in Structural Engineering, fatemeh.azhari@monash.edu Position Description: Postdoctoral Research Fellow Applications Close: Tuesday 27th October 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/696999/senior-technical-officer": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Officer",
      "description": "Senior Technical Officer Job No.: 696999 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: HEW 7 plus 17% super Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join the School of Chemistry and play a key role in supporting world-class research and teaching through the delivery of advanced analytical services. We are seeking an experienced analytical scientist to provide technical leadership and specialist expertise in Mass Spectrometry and Chromatography instrumentation and applications. As a senior member of our analytical services team, you will be responsible for the operation, maintenance, development and continuous improvement of Mass Spectrometry capabilities that support a diverse community of researchers, students and external users. This role offers the opportunity to work across a broad range of analytical challenges while contributing to the strategic development of the School's instrumentation facilities. You will provide expert technical advice, support user training, maintain high standards of safety and compliance, and help ensure the reliable delivery of analytical services. Importantly, this position forms part of a small, highly skilled team of Senior Technical Officers who collectively support the School's analytical infrastructure. While Mass Spectrometry will be your primary area of expertise, you will also work closely with colleagues specialising in NMR, X-ray, Chromatography and Spectroscopy, contribute to a collaborative team environment, and provide support to other facilities as required. About You You will bring: Extensive experience in the operation, maintenance and application of Mass Spectrometry instrumentation in a research, analytical or teaching environment. Broad analytical instrumentation knowledge and a willingness to work across multiple techniques and facilities. Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot complex technical issues and deliver high-quality user support. Strong communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with experience working effectively with researchers, students and external clients. A collaborative approach and the flexibility to support colleagues and shared analytical services across the School. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced analytical scientist who enjoys combining deep technical expertise with teamwork, service delivery and continuous improvement. Together with a dedicated team of analytical specialists, you will help deliver the facilities and expertise that underpin the School's research and teaching success. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. The position is seeking applications that have Australian working rights for the duration of the position. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Tracy McGregor, School Manager, School of Chemistry, +61 3 9905 4310 Position Description: Senior Technical Officer Applications Close: Monday 2nd November, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698813/finance-business-partner": {
      "title": "Finance Business Partner x 2",
      "description": "Finance Business Partner x 2 Job No.: 698813 Location: Mulgrave & St Kilda Road, Melbourne Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 10 month and 13 month fixed-term appointments Remuneration: $110,527 - $121,227 p.a. HEW Level 7 plus 17% employer superannuation Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity We’re seeking an experienced Finance Business Partner to provide high-quality, proactive accounting advisory and support across research and revenue (R&R) activities. Reporting to the Research and Revenue Accounting Services Manager, you’ll provide expert advice on complex financial transactions, research grants and contracts, budgets, forecasts and financial reporting. This is a key business partnering role, working closely with clients and stakeholders to maximise research funding, identify emerging financial issues and provide practical, solutions-focused advice. You’ll also lead and support a team member, building capability through coaching, mentoring and effective work allocation while contributing to continuous improvement across R&R finance services. We’re looking for a commercially minded finance professional with strong financial acumen, analytical and problem-solving skills and the ability to communicate complex financial information clearly to diverse audiences. A relevant finance qualification with current CPA or CA status and significant experience, or an equivalent combination of experience and education, is highly desirable, along with experience using SAP or a similar financial management system. About Research & Revenue Accounting Services (R&R) The Unit supports the University’s research community by delivering end-to-end financial services across the lifecycle of research projects. Managing approximately $700 million in research activity annually, the team provides project costing, contract and funding advice, milestone monitoring, financial management, and reporting. Through close collaboration with researchers, R&R ensures robust financial stewardship while enabling high-impact research outcomes. At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Mr Joe Faisal, Research and Revenue Accounting Services Manager - 03 9905 1220 Position Description: Finance Business Partner Applications Close: Wednesday, 28th October at 11:55pm AEST Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
