    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699641/educational-outreach-officer-expression-of-interest": {
      "title": "Educational Outreach Officer - Expression of Interest",
      "description": "Educational Outreach Officer - Expression of Interest Job Card : 699641 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full time, part time and casual opportunities Duration: Varied Remuneration: Pro-rata of $79,430 - $84,963 pa HEW Level 04 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join the BioEYES Australia program as an Educational Outreach Officer, helping inspire the next generation of scientists through engaging, hands-on science education. Working with the Outreach Education Coordinator and Director of Outreach Education, you will deliver interactive biomedical science programs to primary and secondary students across Melbourne and Victoria, making complex scientific concepts accessible and exciting. In this varied role, you will support the effective delivery of BioEYES through program teaching, administration, teacher professional development workshops, student surveys and ongoing communication with teachers, students and stakeholders. You will also maintain educational equipment and materials, including microscopes and fish, while contributing to program evaluation, reporting and the development of new outreach initiatives. We are seeking an enthusiastic and organised professional with a tertiary qualification in biological or biomedical science and/or teaching, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and training. You will bring strong communication and administrative skills, a commitment to educational excellence, attention to detail and the ability to work collaboratively and independently. If you are passionate about science education and inspiring young learners, we encourage you to apply. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Please note a Drivers licence is a requirement of this position. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Laura Reid, Engagement and Outreach Coordinator +61 3 (9902 0399) Position Description: Educational Outreach Officer Applications Close: Wednesday, 11th November at 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698019/it-service-centre-av-support-officer": {
      "title": "IT Service Centre AV Support Officer",
      "description": "IT Service Centre AV Support Officer Job No.: 698019 Location: Caulfield, City, Peninsula, and Rural Campuses Employment Type: Full-time, with a rotating roster covering standard daytime hours and afternoon shifts (1 pm–9 pm) during teaching periods Duration: Until 30 September 2027 Remuneration: $86,344 - $99,179 pa HEW Level 05 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them Why Join Monash? At Monash, work feels different. We combine world-class research and learning environments with a culture that values work-life balance, diversity, and genuine career development. As part of the eSolutions team, you won't just be fixing gear; you’ll be enabling cutting-edge hybrid learning environments, collaborative research spaces, and high-profile university events. Benefits Market-Leading Superannuation: 17% employer superannuation contribution, boosting your take-home value significantly above commercial standard Work-Life Balance & Predictability: Structured shift hours, protected breaks, clear overtime provisions, and the stability of a leading global institution Convenient Location: Mainly based at our vibrant Caulfield Campus - easy access via public transport with local parking options, saving you the hassle of daily Melbourne CBD travel Broad Tech Exposure: Hands-on experience across state-of-the-art enterprise AV, Crestron/Extron control systems, digital signage, lecture capture, and integrated IT service infrastructure (ITIL / Remedy) The Role Reporting to the Senior IT Service Centre AV Team Leader, you will be a core operational presence on campus, ensuring our AV and learning space technology runs smoothly. Key Responsibilities: Provide front-line technical support (face-to-face and phone) to resolve AV and IT issues in teaching, meeting, and event spaces across campus Act as a trusted subject matter expert for academic staff, professional teams, and students using campus AV systems Diagnose, troubleshoot, and coordinate quick-turnaround repairs for AV control systems, displays, microphones, video conferencing (Teams/Zoom Rooms), and connected desktop systems Log and manage service tickets in Remedy, contributing to continuous service improvement and technical documentation Collaborate across the broader eSolutions team to deliver seamless IT/AV operations About You You thrive in customer-facing technical environments and take pride in keeping systems online and users supported. Whether you come from a commercial AV integration background, live production/events, or an IT service desk, you bring a diagnostic mindset and a passion for helping people. Your Experience & Qualifications: Technical Skills: Sound hands-on knowledge of AV systems (displays, switchers, control systems, audio processing) and standardized desktop hardware/software Customer Focus: Demonstrated commitment to delivering exceptional customer service under operational deadlines. Problem-Solving Ability: Strong analytical skills with a proactive approach to fault-finding Qualifications: Relevant tertiary qualification (with ITIL Foundation preferred), or equivalent substantial hands-on industry experience Compliance & Flexibility: Ability to work standard shift rosters (including 1 pm–9 pm during teaching periods) and hold a valid Victorian Working With Children Check (WWCC) and hold a current Australian driver's licence, as travel between multiple Monash campuses is required About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply If you're ready to bring your AV skills to a vibrant campus community, we want to hear from you! Please submit your resume along with a short cover letter outlining your experience in AV/IT technical support. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and interviews may be conducted on a rolling basis before the advertisement closes. Early applications are encouraged. Please refer to “ How to apply for Monash Jobs ”. This role is a full-time position; however, flexible working arrangements may be negotiated. The availability of AV support is essential from 1pm to 9pm during University teaching periods. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Mr Suman Ramakrishnan, Senior AV Team Leader, +61 459 895 703 Position Description: IT Service Centre AV Support Officer Closing Date: Sunday 22 November 2026, 11:55 pm AEDT* *applications will be reviewed as they are received, and interviews may be conducted on a rolling basis before the advertisement closes. Early applications are encouraged. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698472/research-fellow-ultrafast-modulation-of-reconfigurable-metaphotonics": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Ultrafast modulation of reconfigurable metaphotonics",
      "description": "Research Fellow - Ultrafast modulation of reconfigurable metaphotonics Job No.: 698472 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 2 year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $86,195 - $116,981 pa Level A (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join the School of Physics and Astronomy at Monash University as a Research Fellow, contributing to cutting-edge research in reconfigurable metasurfaces and ultrafast photonics. The Research Fellow will work on developing a reconfigurable metasurface platform using phase-change materials and investigating its temporal modulation through an ultrafast pump–probe optical system. The research will explore laser-induced phase transitions in low-loss phase-change materials, alongside ultrafast carrier-driven modulation in semiconductor platforms, advancing new approaches to dynamic photonic technologies. About You To be considered for this position, you will have: A doctoral qualification (PhD) in a relevant discipline or a closely related field. Research experience relevant to the development of reconfigurable metasurfaces, phase-change materials or ultrafast photonics. This is a genuine opportunity to deepen your expertise in an area where materials science, nanophotonics and ultrafast optics converge — working alongside researchers in one of Australia's leading physics schools, with access to the facilities and collaborative networks that serious experimental photonics demands. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Your application should include: A resume ( No longer than 2 pages ) a response addressing the Key Selection Criteria (KSC) from the PD For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Dr Haoran Ren, Senior Lecturer, School of Physics and Astronomy, +61 406 981 830 Position Description: Research Fellow Applications Close: Monday 23 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699030/hsw-business-partner": {
      "title": "HSW Business Partner",
      "description": "HSW Business Partner Job No.: 699030 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: $124,343 - $137,251 pa HEW Level 08 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Monash University is seeking an HSW Business Partner to serve as a trusted strategic advisor across assigned faculties, divisions or schools. In this role, you will partner with senior leaders, staff and students to deliver authoritative safety advice, shape risk management strategies and foster a proactive culture of physical and psychological wellbeing within our ISO 45001-accredited framework. Reporting to the Manager HSW, you will lead complex hazard investigations, analyse safety metrics to produce executive briefings and deliver targeted training workshops. You will also build strong consultative networks with safety committees, Health & Safety Representatives, and key partners like HR and Security to ensure consistent, high-quality service delivery and continuous process improvement across the university. To succeed, you hold postgraduate qualifications in HSW (or equivalent experience) paired with a strong track record of strategic partnering in a large, complex organisation. You possess exceptional consulting, analytical and communication skills, deep knowledge of relevant safety legislation and a strong understanding of the contemporary HSW landscape in the tertiary sector. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 stu