    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698990/research-support-officer": {
      "title": "Research Support Officer",
      "description": "Research Support Officer Job No.: 698990 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: 0.6 - 1.0 FTE Duration: 6-months fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $79,430 - $84,963 pa HEW Level 4 (plus 17% superannuation) (pro-rata for part-time) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity We are seeking a Research Assistant to provide administrative, operational and research support to the Stamatakis research group, led by Professor Emmanuel Stamatakis in the School of Psychological Sciences. The group is based at BrainPark (Clayton campus) and undertakes translational research on how movement, sleep and other everyday behaviours shape cardiovascular, brain and mental health, using wearable technologies and advanced data science. We would particularly welcome expressions of interest from current Monash staff in administrative or research support roles who are looking to initiate a new role or pick up additional part-time hours. The person employed in the position will work directly with Associate Professor Matthew Ahmadi, Mrs Meghna Pathak, Professor Emmanuel Stamatakis, and members of the research group. The role has a strong administrative focus. What you’ll do: Organising and scheduling meetings, managing calendars, and preparing agendas and minutes Coordinating research events, seminars, travel and bookings Processing purchase requests, invoices and reimbursements, and maintaining records of project expenditure Supporting research project administration, including ethics documentation, approvals and progress reports Assisting with formatting and referencing manuscripts, reports and presentations Supporting participant recruitment and scheduling, and maintaining participant databases Maintaining laboratory supplies and supporting the booking and tracking of wearable devices Assisting with onboarding and day-to-day administrative support for research students and new staff Other administrative and research support responsibilities, as per the Team’s needs The successful applicant will have a diploma-level qualification with relevant work experience, or an equivalent combination of experience and/or education/training. Strong administration and organisational skills, excellent attention to detail and a commitment to high-quality customer service are essential. Experience in a university or research environment is highly desirable. Familiarity with Monash systems and processes (e.g. purchasing, travel and event booking) would be an advantage, as would a willingness to learn new software, including reference management and AI productivity tools. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply The position description is attached. To apply, please submit a brief cover letter outlining your suitability for the role against the key selection criteria, your current CV, and your preferred FTE and availability. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Position Description: Research Support Officer Enquiries: Associate Professor Matthew Ahmadi at matthew.ahmadi@monash.edu or Mrs Meghna Pathak (meghna.pathak@monash.edu). Applications Close: Sunday 1 November 2026, 11:55PM AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/696873/primary-care-project-officer": {
      "title": "Primary Care Project Officer",
      "description": "Primary Care Project Officer Job No.: 696873 Location: 509 St Kilda Road, Melbourne Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.4) Duration: 12-month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $86,344 - $99,179 pa HEW Level 05 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join Monash University’s Department of General Practice as a Primary Care Project Officer and support the delivery and ongoing development of the Monash Research and Education Network (MonREN). You’ll coordinate projects, stakeholder engagement, meetings, workshops and education activities, working with general practices, researchers, health services and communities to strengthen primary care research and the translation of evidence into practice. You’ll also contribute to primary care initiatives delivered in partnership with Monash Partners, supporting collaboration, health service integration and strategic activities across the region. With a focus on high-quality project coordination and administration, you’ll help deliver initiatives that build primary care research capacity and support meaningful outcomes for health services and communities. About You You’ll be an organised and collaborative project professional with experience coordinating projects and managing competing priorities within agreed timeframes. You’ll bring strong organisational, analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and build productive relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. You’ll also have excellent written and verbal communication skills, with experience preparing reports, presentations and professional documentation. Experience or understanding of primary care, health services, health research or research translation will be highly regarded, as will knowledge of implementation science, practice-based research networks or health system collaboration. Please apply as soon as possible, as applications will be reviewed and candidates may be interviewed during the advertising period. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This role requires current valid work rights for Australia. Monash University invites applications from candidates who can demonstrate valid and current Australian work rights. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Emiko Hunt, MonREN Network Manager | Clinical Trials Coordinator - CONSEP, Department of General Practice, School of Public Health and Preventive Medicine, emiko.hunt@monash.edu Position Description: Primary Care Project Officer Applications Close: Tuesday 3 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698803/lecturer-education-focused-midwifery": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Education Focused) in Midwifery",
      "description": "Lecturer (Education Focused) in Midwifery Job No.: 698803 Location: Clayton or Peninsula campus Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.6) Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: Pro-rata of $123,138 - $146,228 pa Level B (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact as a Lecturer (Midwifery – Education-focused) at Monash Join an inclusive, collaborative community advancing midwifery education Be inspired by extraordinary ideas shaping complex care midwifery practice The Opportunity Join Monash University as a Lecturer (Midwifery – Education-focused) and contribute to the design and delivery of innovative, evidence-informed education. This exciting opportunity will support the development of future midwives through engaging undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, with a specialist focus on complex care midwifery within the Master of Advanced Midwifery. The position will contribute to curriculum and unit development, teaching delivery, assessment and unit coordination across undergraduate and postgraduate courses. Through collaboration with clinical partners and academic colleagues, the role will foster inclusive, student-centred learning environments, enhance teaching practice and contribute to educational scholarship. There will also be opportunities to lead teaching initiatives, supervise postgraduate research and use student feedback to continually improve the learning experience. We are seeking someone with a Master’s degree or doctoral qualification in midwifery or nursing, a postgraduate qualification in complex care midwifery and/or critical care nursing and current NMBA registration as a Midwife or Registered Nurse and Midwife. The ideal candidate will bring relevant clinical experience in complex care midwifery, tertiary or clinical teaching experience, curriculum development skills and a track record of educational or clinical leadership, supported by strong communication and collaboration skills, a commitment to scholarly activity and the ability to engage and motivate students. If you are passionate about advancing midwifery education and preparing practitioners to deliver complex care, we encourage you to apply. Monash University seeks applicants for this opportunity who are able to demonstrate present valid and current Australian work rights. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground-breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . This position will require working on campus/s on a weekly basis. To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Wendy Pollock,+ 61 3 9905 0010 Position Description: Lecturer (Education Focused) Midwifery Applications Close: Thursday 19 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
