    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699580/student-support-officer": {
      "title": "Student Support Officer",
      "description": "Student Support Officer Job No.: 699580 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Casual part time, 22 hours per week, from 2 Nov 2026 - 29 Jan 2027 Remuneration: Casual HEW 5 rates will apply Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join the Faculty of Arts as a casual Student Support Officer, delivering high-quality administrative services and support throughout the student lifecycle. You will assist students with enquiries, course advice, enrolments, course progression, completions, transfers and academic progress, helping them navigate their studies with confidence. Working collaboratively with colleagues and key stakeholders, you will provide timely advice and responsive customer service while ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. You will also contribute to continuous improvement initiatives that enhance service delivery, streamline processes and improve the student experience. About You You are a customer-focused and organised professional with strong administrative skills and a commitment to delivering accurate, timely and high-quality service. You communicate effectively, provide clear and helpful advice, and can manage competing priorities while maintaining attention to detail and confidentiality. You enjoy working collaboratively with a diverse range of stakeholders and building positive working relationships. With a proactive approach to problem-solving and continuous improvement, you are committed to contributing to a supportive team culture and delivering an excellent student experience. Please apply as soon as possible, as applications will be reviewed and candidates may be interviewed during the advertising period. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great 