    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699120/senior-animal-technologist": {
      "title": "Senior Animal Technologist",
      "description": "Senior Animal Technologist Job No.: 699120 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: $100,155 - $108,106 pa HEW Level 06 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join MARP as a Senior Animal Technologist and use your technical expertise to support world-class research while upholding the highest standards of laboratory animal care and welfare. In this hands-on technical role, you’ll deliver specialised animal care and research support services, manage daily activities within a designated unit, and assist in coordinating workloads and resources. You’ll provide guidance, training and supervision to junior staff, support researchers, and drive improvements in animal welfare, operational efficiency and compliance. You’ll also apply your technical expertise to oversee technical procedures, maintain high standards of animal care and build strong working relationships with colleagues and stakeholders. We are seeking an experienced and motivated senior animal technology professional with strong technical knowledge, excellent organisational and communication skills, and a commitment to animal welfare and continuous improvement. A Diploma of Animal Technology or equivalent qualifications and experience is required. About MARP - Monash Animal Research Platform MARP is committed to enabling excellence in research by providing industry-leading animal services to Monash University researchers and partners across Australia. Guided by best-practice animal care and a culture of continuous improvement, MARP offers an outstanding environment in which expertise, innovation, and collaboration thrive. Learn more about MARP About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to somethin