    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698857/program-manager": {
      "title": "Program Manager",
      "description": "Program Manager Job No.: 698857 Location: The Alfred Centre Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.6) Duration: 12-month fixed term appointment Remuneration: $124,343 - $137,251 pa HEW Level 08 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Carbapenemase-producing Enterobacterales represent one of Australia's most serious and rising antibiotic resistance threats. STOP-CPE is a $3.9 million Medical Research Future Fund program bringing together eleven Chief Investigators, nine partner institutions, and clinical sites across four states — and this part-time, fixed-term role keeps it all moving. What the Role Involves Serve as the central coordination point across multi-site research activities, governance committees, and partner organisations Establish and manage the governance framework, including secretariat support to the Steering Committee, Working Groups, Consumer Advisory Group, and Data Management Committee Coordinate HREC and institutional ethics applications, research contracts, subcontracts, and data-sharing agreements in liaison with Monash Research Office and partner institutions Monitor MRFF milestones and budgets up to $2.9M, preparing progress reports and maintaining financial forecasts and risk registers What You Bring Postgraduate qualification in health, public health, biomedical science, research management, or a related discipline Demonstrated experience coordinating multi-site health or clinical research programs Hands-on experience preparing and submitting HREC applications and working within National Statement and GCP frameworks Strong financial management skills, including budget monitoring, expenditure tracking, and grant compliance reporting Experience managing research contracts and collaborative partnerships across institutions — ideally within a Monash or university research environment Clear, confident communication across multidisciplinary teams including consumer representatives and policy stakeholders Why This Program Based at The Alfred Centre, you'll work at the intersection of policy, advocacy, and scientific innovation on a nationally significant program. Monash University offers generous above-SGC superannuation, substantial leave entitlements, and a genuine commitment to research integrity and inclusive practice. The work is complex, the team is expert, and the outcomes have real consequence for Australian healthcare. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Please address the Key Selection criteria within your Cover Letter. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Dr Nenad Maćešić, Senior Research Fellow, Dept. of Infectious Diseases and Deputy Director, Centre to Impact AMR - nenad.macesic1@monash.edu Position Description: Program Manager Applications Close: Tuesday 3 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698674/associate-professor-of-architecture-and-deputy-head-of-department": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Architecture and Deputy Head of Department",
      "description": "Associate Professor of Architecture and Deputy Head of Department Job No.: 698674 Location: Caulfield campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: Competitive remuneration package will apply Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them Join the Department of Architecture within the Faculty of Art, Design and Architecture (MADA) as an Associate Professor and Deputy Head of Department, contributing to excellence in education, research, creative practice and engagement. Working closely with the Head of Department, you will provide internal academic leadership, support staff development and coordinate the people, processes and resources needed to deliver the Department’s strategic priorities. This is an opportunity for an accomplished architectural academic or practitioner with strong organisational judgement, a collaborative approach and a commitment to strengthening the culture and performance of an ambitious department. You will work with Course Directors, program leaders, unit coordinators and professional staff to support coherent curricula and high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Your responsibilities will include coordinating academic workload and staffing plans, teaching resources and space planning, alongside assessment, moderation, program review and professional accreditation processes. The role also supports a productive research and creative-practice culture through collaboration, mentoring, postgraduate supervision and the development of external funding and partnerships. You will supervise and mentor allocated staff, contribute to career development and workload equity, and help address complex staff and student matters through appropriate University processes. As Deputy Head, you will support the implementation of departmental strategy, contribute to budget and resource planning, represent the Department when delegated, and act on behalf of the Head of Department under formally approved arrangements. Alongside these leadership responsibilities, you will sustain a significant contribution to teaching, research and disciplinary practice appropriate to a Level D academic appointment. The successful candidate will hold a doctoral qualification in architecture or a relevant discipline, or have recognised significant professional experience and standing in architecture or the built environment. You will bring a strong record of scholarly, creative-practice or professional achievement; demonstrated teaching excellence; experience in academic leadership and operational coordination; and the ability to build consensus and implement academic change. Excellent interpersonal skills and a commitment to collegiality, inclusion and staff and student development are essential. The professorial appointment will be a continuing appointment in the department of Architecture and will include the role of Deputy head of department for an initial period of up to 3 years with opportunity for renewal. About the Department of Architecture The Department of Architecture is a globally connected community offering undergraduate and postgraduate programs in Architecture and Urban Planning and Design. Planning Our research and teaching converge around some of the most urgent issues of our time: advancing housing, social and environmental justice, innovating construction processes for accessibility and affordability, addressing the challenges of informal settlements and environmental repair, radically reducing carbon emissions and energy use, and imagining new spatial, technological, and cultural futures for the planet. Combining scholarship with creative practice, we approach architecture as an agent of change, shaping a world that is more just, sustainable and beautiful. Through our distinctive model of creative-practice impact, the Department of Architecture at Monash University tackles the major challenges facing society today with innovation, impact, and criticality. Our work is animated by a belief that architecture can be an agent of change—shaping a world that is more just, sustainable, and beautiful. Together with our commitment to academic freedom, you will have access to quality research facilities, teaching spaces and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about the Department of Architecture: monash.edu/mada/architecture About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Your application will include: Current CV A cover letter addressing the 7 Key Selection Criterias (document here) (No more than 3 pages) Portfolio if applicable For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Erik L'Heureux (PhD) FAIA, Head, Department of Architecture, erik.lheureux@monash.edu Position Description: Associate Professor and Deputy Head of Department Applications Close: Tuesday 1 December 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699361/education-programs-and-delivery-manager": {
      "title": "Education Programs and Delivery Manager",
      "description": "Education Programs and Delivery Manager Job No.: 699361 Location: Caulfield campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Fixed-term appointment from 05/01/27 to 30/06/27 Remuneration: $124,343 - $137,251 HEW 8 plus 17% employer superannuation Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join the Monash Business School as our Education Programs and Delivery Manager, where you will play a key role in shaping and delivering a high-quality coursework portfolio. Leading a team of four, you will work closely with senior academic leaders and professional staff to support education strategy, strengthen quality and compliance, and enhance the delivery of education programs across the School. You will oversee course and unit development, governance and quality assurance, ensuring course information is accurate and education processes run smoothly. From managing operational requirements across learning platforms and student management systems to resolving complex policy and course design challenges, you will drive continuous improvement and build strong partnerships across the University to support an excellent education experience. About You You are an experienced manager who thrives in a complex environment and enjoys bringing people together to deliver high-quality outcomes. With a strong customer focus and experience leading and developing teams, you know how to manage competing priorities, improve processes and provide trusted advice on operational and policy matters. You bring highly developed analytical, planning and communication skills, with the confidence to navigate complex challenges, influence senior stakeholders and build collaborative relationships. From managing operational requirements across learning platforms and student management systems to resolving complex policy and course design challenges, you will drive continuous improvement and build strong partnerships across the University to support an excellent education experience. Your knowledge of academic administration and the Australian tertiary education sector, combined with experience across core enterprise platforms, will enable you to make a valuable contribution to the School’s education programs and services. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This role requires current valid work rights for Australia. Monash University invites applications from candidates who can demonstrate valid and current Australian work rights. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Fiona Bertoli, Education Services Manager, +61 3 990 32074 Position Description: Education Programs and Delivery Manager Applications Close: Monday 2nd of November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
