    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699550/research-nurse-oncology": {
      "title": "Research Nurse (Oncology)",
      "description": "Research Nurse (Oncology) Job No.: 699550 Location: Box Hill Hospital Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $110,527 - $121,227 pa HEW Level 07 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Research Nurse (Oncology) will play a vital role in advancing clinical research at Monash University, coordinating oncology clinical trials that contribute to improved understanding and treatment of cancer. Working within a multidisciplinary team, you will combine your clinical nursing expertise with research coordination to deliver high-quality, participant-centred care, support the collection of robust research data and ensure trials are conducted safely, ethically and in accordance with professional and regulatory standards. This position will be responsible for coordinating the delivery of clinical research trials, from participant recruitment, screening and informed consent through to trial visits, clinical assessments, ongoing monitoring and follow-up care. You will collect, analyse and maintain accurate research data, manage clinical trial records and databases, and provide education and support to participants throughout their involvement. Working closely with investigators, hospital and clinical teams, pharmaceutical companies and external research partners, you will build strong stakeholder relationships and contribute to research administration, reporting and publications. You will also support the development of research procedures, quality assurance and continuous improvement initiatives, ensuring all activities comply with ethical, privacy, confidentiality, Good Clinical Practice and relevant regulatory requirements. To be successful in this role you will have current registration as a Registered Nurse with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia, alongside demonstrated clinical nursing experience in a relevant field, such as oncology or haematology. You will bring strong clinical assessment, problem-solving and care coordination skills, supported by excellent organisational abilities and the capacity to manage competing priorities. An understanding of human research ethics, Good Clinical Practice, informed consent and clinical trial protocols is essential. You will demonstrate sound judgement, initiative and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, computer literacy, meticulous documentation practices and a clear understanding of patient confidentiality are also key, together with the ability to recognise and promptly escalate clinical concerns and adverse events. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Karen Lim, Clinical Trials Team Leader, +61 3 9094 9564 Position Description: Research Nurse Applications Close: Thursday 12 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699276/research-officer": {
      "title": "Research Officer",
      "description": "Research Officer Job No.: 699276 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12 month appointment Remuneration: $86,344 - $99,179 p.a. HEW Level 6 plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Mitochondrial Biology, Metabolism and Disease Lab is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Research Officer to support research activities through laboratory experiments, data collection and analysis, troubleshooting, research documentation and general laboratory administration. Reporting to the Head of the Lab, the successful candidate will contribute to research outcomes while maintaining a safe, compliant and well-organised laboratory environment. The role involves supporting research projects, conducting literature reviews, preparing reports, maintaining accurate records and contributing to continuous improvement in research procedures. The Research Officer will also collaborate with researchers and students, stay up to date with developments in the field, and ensure compliance with research protocols, quality standards and safety requirements. Applicants will have a relevant qualification or equivalent experience, with skills in cell culture, molecular biology (PCR, vector cloning) and/or protein chemistry (SDS-PAGE, western transfer). Experience in proteomics, confocal imaging or flow cytometry is advantageous. Strong analytical, organisational, communication and data management skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively are essential. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Luke Formosa, Senior Lecturer, +61 3 9902 9369 Position Description: Research Officer Applications Close: Thursday, 19th November at 11:55pm AEDT Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699409/workshop-and-stores-technical-officer": {
      "title": "Workshop and Stores Technical Officer",
      "description": "Workshop and Stores Technical Officer Job No.: 699408 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $86,344 - $99,179 p.a. HEW Level 5 plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Monash University’s Maintenance Technology Institute (MTI) is seeking a skilled Workshop and Stores Technical Officer to support its research programs through the design, fabrication, assembly, modification and repair of specialised equipment and bespoke components. Ideal for a qualified Fitter and Turner, Toolmaker or Machinist, this hands-on role combines technical manufacturing expertise with workshop and stores management. We are looking for a proactive self-starter who can think on their feet, solve technical problems and work independently with minimal supervision. Responsibilities include machining and fabrication, equipment maintenance and troubleshooting, inventory management, procurement, and coordinating equipment preparation and dispatch to operational sites. You will bring strong manufacturing skills, sound problem-solving abilities and excellent organisational skills, with a commitment to safety, quality and teamwork. If you enjoy taking ownership, finding practical solutions and applying your trade expertise to support innovative research, we encourage you to apply. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Australian working rights are required for the duration of this contract. Please address the following Key selection criteria points within your cover letter - KSC#2, #3 and #5 along with your relevant Trade experience/certificate. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries : Mr Stelios Konstantinidis, Business Manager (MTI), + 61 3 9905 3430 Position Description: Workshop and Stores Technical Officer Applications Close: Monday 16 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    }
